(Challenge: Solar Cell Voltage Matrix) Tj
T* (The Engineering Block solar array monitors panels in a square grid of size $N × N$.) Tj
T* (Due to shadow occlusions, panel readings must be balanced by calculating the sum of values on both primary and secondary diagonals.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Write a function `solve\(grid\)` that takes an $N × N$ 2D array of numbers and returns the sum of all elements lying on either the main) Tj
T* (diagonal or the anti-diagonal. If an element lies at the center intersection \(odd $N$\), count it only once.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Example:) Tj
T* () Tj
T* ([[1, 2, 3],) Tj
T* ( [4, 5, 6],) Tj
T* ( [7, 8, 9]]) Tj
