(Challenge: Auditorium Audio Filter) Tj
T* (The auditorium digital audio console registers sound pressure waveforms. In acoustic analysis, peaks above a noise floor threshold $T$) Tj
T* (must be normalized.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Write a function `solve\(readings, threshold\)` that accepts an array of positive decibel numbers and a threshold $T$:) Tj
T* (1. Filters out all readings strictly below threshold $T$.) Tj
T* (2. For all remaining readings, scales them: $\\text{scaled} = \(v - T\)^2$.) Tj
T* (3. Returns the integer sum of all scaled values.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Example:) Tj
T* (* Input: `\([40, 65, 80, 50, 95], 60\)`) Tj
T* (* Filtered \($\\ge 60$\): `[65, 80, 95]`) Tj
T* (* Scaled:) Tj
T* (  * $\(65 - 60\)^2 = 25$) Tj
T* (  * $\(80 - 60\)^2 = 400$) Tj
T* (  * $\(95 - 60\)^2 = 1225$) Tj
T* (* Sum: $25 + 400 + 1225 = 1650$) Tj
ET
